PASS C0 place(sig, (0,1), rho) == sig (x) rho (symbolic)
PASS C0 PT is an involution on every qubit (symbolic 8 x 8)
PASS C0 PT is self-adjoint for the pairing tr(A B) (symbolic)
PASS C0 PT permutes entries, so it preserves the Hilbert-Schmidt norm
PASS T1 every generator's pair marginals lie in that pair's cone: PT^t(sigma) on the matching pair, a product of one-copy marginals on the others (symbolic, both twists, all pairs)
PASS T2 conditioning on an effect: the matching pair gives a multiple of PT^t(sigma), a copy of the pair gives a product (symbolic)
PASS T3 COMP-1 on pair|single, mismatched generators: <E (x) f, g> = tr(E_rho . sigma_f) with one-copy operators E_rho (E contracted with the state g carries) and sigma_f (g's pair operator contracted with f) (symbolic)
PASS T4 control: the three Cayley transforms are exactly unitary
PASS T4 IE1: (U (x) V (x) X) maps the generator family of each pair onto itself, PT_j intertwining U_j with conj U_j (symbolic sigma, rho; exact rational unitaries)
PASS T5 per-token chart: PT on copy q flips the twist bit of each pair containing q (image = PT_j^(1-t) of a transpose of sigma, still PSD) and transposes the state of a copy outside the pair (symbolic)
PASS T6 a per-token chart presenting all three pairs as Q exists iff t01 + t02 + t12 is even (all 8 tau); M_odd = K_(0,1,0) and M_tw = K_(1,1,1) have none, M_bs = K_(0,0,0) has the trivial one
PASS G1 omega0 = |+><+|_0 (x) Phi+_(1,2) is the generator 'Phi+ on (1,2) times |+> on 0' (Kronecker form)
PASS G2 (CNOT_(0,1) (x) 1) omega0 (CNOT (x) 1)^dag = |GHZ'><GHZ'| exactly
PASS G3 W' = 1/2 - |GHZ'><GHZ'| has value tr(W' GHZ') = -1/2
PASS G3 input of the written bound: every one-copy marginal of GHZ' is 1/2
PASS G3 control: CNOT maps the pair cone Q onto itself (unitary conjugation); t01 = 0 in M_odd and M_bs
